 "notes": [
  "Windows scored per split (after the frozen no-data-frame filter): {\"test\": 1631, \"case_holdout\": 306}; 3 windows per SEVIR event at offsets 0/12/24 frames.",
  "Primary csi_mean_74_133 = mean over thresholds 74 and 133 of the lead-averaged CSI (12 leads, 5-60 min), contingency counts pooled over all windows and pixels per lead. CSI/FSS/MSE use the U-Net VIL regression head x 255 (clipped); persistence = last observed VIL frame; pysteps_extrapolation = Lucas-Kanade motion + semi-Lagrangian advection of the last frame (baselines.extrapolation_nowcast), VIL-only inputs.",
  "CIs: day-block bootstrap over UTC event days (seed 0, same resamples for every model, so models are paired), 1000 resamples. Sample = window; days are SEVIR event start days.",
  "Brier and ECE (10 equal-width bins, pooled over leads) are for the calibrated P(VIL >= 133) head of the U-Nets only (the frozen per-lead isotonic calibrators were fit on val; val calibration numbers are therefore optimistic). Baselines have no probabilities, so no Brier/ECE.",
  "Ablation 'vil_only' = models/storm_vil_only (13 VIL channels, no IR107), evaluated on the same windows and with its own frozen val calibrator; extra splits are keyed 'vil_only@<split>'.",
  "Not done: the 1 km resolution check and the storm-windows subset listed in DESIGN 6.1; pooling means windows with little weather weigh little in CSI (pooled counts), as in the val runs.",
  "models/storm_run1 (earlier run) is ignored."
